e siege without a fight), invisible monsters for Bee clients, the builder hidden in the opening area, x-ray missing, audio silenced after the attract mode, and oversized saves.\",\n    \"The scripted playthrough with the Autopilot: it plays the real systems end to end and found the out-of-reach targeting, border placement and pickup problems no unit check would.\",\n    \"The early world-generation determinism check: it never failed and only confirmed what the design already guaranteed.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Its views are plain linear projections with exact whole-pixel control, so a voxel renderer could plug straight into its depth-sorted queue, x-ray, lighting and particles; the Humanoid rigs, dialog, menus, saves and settings came for free.\",\n    \"Yes: queued occluders need a screen box for the x-ray pass, which I only found by reading the flush code; and the default iso view's height step is not a whole number of pixels, so I made my own views.\",\n    \"The voxel world: storage, a face-sprite atlas renderer with column runs, cutaway and water, circle-body physics with stairs, and A* navigation, because the engine's TileMap is a heightmap.\",\n    \"Depth sorting real 3D blocks with a 2D painter's queue built for heightmap walls: lifting actors over the blocks they stand on and keeping roofs in front.\",\n    \"Small, marked // DQB: an input wheelSteps() accessor that works while the camera wheel is off and a right-stick flick(), a Dialog onLetter hook for per-letter voices, a Voices audio bus, and tool kinds (stick, club, Seam Ripper) drawn on the Humanoid's sword joints.\",\n    \"A first-class block or voxel map type with its own lift hook and occluder boxes, so 3D building games do not have to rebuild the renderer.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"A clear definition of done and a detailed plan: every system had a place, and the controller-first, 10-foot rules made the UI decisions easy.\",\n    \"The plan's file names used a different model and timestamp than TASK.md; TASK.md wins, but it took a moment to be sure.\",\n    \"Making a whole chapter completable through real triggers and proving it with an automated playthrough, alongside netcode and an attract mode, in one pass.\",\n    \"Ask for a smaller vertical slice or allow staged delivery; the plan's scope (17 quests, two bosses, a siege, online co-op, an attract mode) is very large for one session.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Dragon Quilt Builders\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Stitch a frayed world back together\",\n    \"description\": \"Gather, craft and build block by block to mend a patchwork kingdom unravelled by a dragon. Raise rooms for quirky residents, defend your town and unpick a knotted boss, or raise a barn together in co-op Quilting Bee rounds.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"RPG\",\n    \"source\": \"Dragon Quest Builders\",\n    \"series\": \"Dragon Quest\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · ✕/Space jump · □/Click break · △/Right-click place · L1 R1/wheel items · ○/F talk\",\n    \"tags\": [\"building\", \"crafting\", \"co-op\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"]\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AcMUEtiTxCGxL7FoQcf4RM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
