{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghU7eBww7Zy5uqz4n41w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AJzLcruU7cdPUf6DRm7L9o","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"41 issues, tallied from this session: 31 bugs in the game and its AI, and 10 mistakes in the tests themselves. Game bugs: x-ray silhouettes missing (wall items had no screen box); the deep Lint Hollow hid the player; the Quilters' Hall room failed on uneven ground; the attract mode silenced all audio, collided with a prop, left the finale cutscene running and left its builder seated on a ballista; stair lips blocked walking; the deep-water rule was wrong; Spin Stitch could not charge; room hints picked a wall-top area; Gnarlgrim could walk into the Rift's void; Rift spawns stuck behind the void; saves stored every plant; Bee clients never saw monsters (a duplicate method name); the version label showed '?'; the Knot Wall towered at full height; damaged blocks healed between hits (a seconds-vs-hours mix-up); M12 needed a far turn-in; 'survive 3 waves' only counted after the boss; the ballista aim arc was too narrow, its bolts hit walls and fell short, and any hit (even zero damage) knocked the player off it; skipping the finale never showed the results; and seven Autopilot faults (out-of-reach spots, chasing monsters across the map, a talk loop that never yielded, not equipping crafted weapons, ignoring the Knot Cage, not clearing plants, residents in the way).\",\n \"8 were game breaking for a player: the Hall room not forming (softlocks quest M10), damaged blocks healing between hits (mining could become impossible), Gnarlgrim falling into the void (the siege ends without its boss), the ballista dismount on any hit (the boss nearly impossible to Tangle), the results never showing after a skipped finale, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the player hidden in the opening area, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\",\n \"The scripted playthrough with the Autopilot: it plays the real systems from New Game to Chapter Clear and found the block-healing, ballista, siege-flow and finale bugs that no single-system check caught.\",\n \"The world-generation determinism check: it never failed and only confirmed what the design already guaranteed.\"\n]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\njson.load(open(p)); print('ok', len(d['testingFeedback']))\nEOF\ncd DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-215911 && node tools/build.mjs --release && node tests/run.mjs --browser 2>&1 | tail -3","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":268,"cache_read_input_tokens":859994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":268},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2","uuid":"36a06d53-a3fe-4446-b07e-701c477ebcbd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:09:33.830Z","request_id":"req_011CghU7dndRKGpnQbZi4iWA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AJzLcruU7cdPUf6DRm7L9o":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-215911__x5b1962/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"41 issues, tallied from this session: 31 bugs in the game and its AI, and 10 mistakes in the tests themselves. Game bugs: x-ray silhouettes missing (wall items had no screen box); the deep Lint Hollow hid the player; the Quilters' Hall room failed on uneven ground; the attract mode silenced all audio, collided with a prop, left the finale cutscene running and left its builder seated on a ballista; stair lips blocked walking; the deep-water rule was wrong; Spin Stitch could not charge; room hints picked a wall-top area; Gnarlgrim could walk into the Rift's void; Rift spawns stuck behind the void; saves stored every plant; Bee clients never saw monsters (a duplicate method name); the version label showed '?'; the Knot Wall towered at full height; damaged blocks healed between hits (a seconds-vs-hours mix-up); M12 needed a far turn-in; 'survive 3 waves' only counted after the boss; the ballista aim arc was too narrow, its bolts hit walls and fell short, and any hit (even zero damage) knocked the player off it; skipping the finale never showed the results; and seven Autopilot faults (out-of-reach spots, chasing monsters across the map, a talk loop that never yielded, not equipping crafted weapons, ignoring the Knot Cage, not clearing plants, residents in the way).\",\n \"8 were game breaking for a player: the Hall room not forming (softlocks quest M10), damaged blocks healing between hits (mining could become impossible), Gnarlgrim falling into the void (the siege ends without its boss), the ballista dismount on any hit (the boss nearly impossible to Tangle), the results never showing after a skipped finale, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the player hidden in the opening area, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\",\n \"The scripted playthrough with the Autopilot: it plays the real systems from New Game to Chapter Clear and found the block-healing, ballista, siege-flow and finale bugs that no single-system check caught.\",\n \"The world-generation determinism check: it never failed and only confirmed what the design already guaranteed.\"\n]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\njson.load(open(p)); print('ok', len(d['testingFeedback']))\nEOF\ncd DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-215911 && node tools/build.mjs --release && node tests/run.mjs --browse