{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghUzbgogoPwJLtx72EXg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The items you named now have passing checks of their own, and the final run after the last edit was 352 passed, 0 failed, including the browser checks. The search for TODO/FIXME/XXX/placeholder/stub/\"not implemented\" found nothing, and `exit-interview.json` parses.\n\n- **Quilted Vest and Copper Buckler** (new checks): both craft, both equip from the hotbar for Def +7, and armour lowers the damage taken.\n- **Debug tab** (new checks): it switches on all seven overlays, sets the time scale and switches the cutaway mode. A new browser check draws a real frame at a built-up town with every overlay on, with no errors.\n- **World tab** (new checks): a dev snapshot saves, loading it restores the world, and \"Regenerate the world\" starts a fresh one. The stamp export and re-import already had passing checks.\n- **Heartpatch and solo Bee bots:** these were already covered in the playthrough and Bee suites. \"Using a Heartpatch raises max HP\" and \"bots place barn blocks and score\" both pass.\n- **Bee win and Knot Cutter:**\n  - The Bee win check was changed during the work. The test now kills raid monsters during the build minute instead of leaving the raid unattended; the win condition itself is unchanged.\n  - The Knot Cutter award check was added late.\n  - Both have passed in every run since, including the final one.\n\nThe game `DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-215911.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 21:59:11\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building, real-time combat, a siege and bosses), seen in third-person isometric 2.5D over a true voxel world. The camera turns in 90° steps and zooms; a three-quarter view is a setting.\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, lightly modified, plus my own voxel world, renderer, physics and pathfinding, in plain ES2020 JavaScript on Canvas 2D and Web Audio.\n  - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (client session.js 1.4.0).\n  - Node 18+ for the headless tests and Playwright 1.63.0 for the browser checks.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel style with an original patchwork-quilt look: stitched fabric-patch blocks, felt menu panels with running-stitch borders, a patchwork logo.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and moves, plus new moves, poses, tools drawn on the rig, boss wind-ups, doors, banner, portals and an unravel effect.\n- **Audio:** all in code: 14 original songs on a leitmotif, 12 jingles, about 50 sound effects, and Animalese voices for each character with their own Voices volume setting.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for the Quilting Bee co-op round (the game's own card, a host-run world, standings, awards, time-up, leave, end and server mode). The same round plays solo with bots outside the hub.\n- **Testing:** headless scripted tests in 19 suites plus browser checks (352 checks in all), including the full playthrough and a fake multi-copy hub with latency and loss; Playwright screenshots; the hub harness's four scenarios.\n- **Research:** no web research on the source game. I read the engine's documentation and source sections, and the AI Hub protocol README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** estimated from the session log:\n  - Tokens: about 122.7M over 208 calls (121.3M cache reads, 0.86M cache writes, 0.56M output).\n  - Cost: about $80 at Opus-class list prices; this model's exact rate is unconfirmed.\n  - Session time: about 2 h 20 min.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 41: 31 bugs in the game and its AI player, and 10 mistakes in the tests themselves.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 8: the Quilters' Hall not forming, damaged blocks healing between hits, Gnarlgrim falling into the void, any hit knocking the player off the ballista, no results screen after a skipped finale, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the player hidden in the opening area, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough from New Game to Chapter Clear.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the world-generation determinism check, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the views are exact linear projections, so a voxel renderer plugged straight into the engine's depth-sorted queue, x-ray, lighting and particles. The rigs, dialog, menus, saves and settings came free.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. Wall items need a screen box for the x-ray pass, which I only found in the source. The default isometric view's block height isn't a whole number of pixels, so I made my own views.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the voxel world: storage, a renderer with cutaway and water, body physics with stairs, and pathfinding.\n4. **Hardest part of the engine:** depth-sorting real 3D blocks in a 2D painter's queue designed for heightmap walls.\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why** (each change marked `// DQB:`):\n   - A mouse-wheel accessor that works while the camera wheel is off, so the wheel can cycle the hotbar.\n   - A right-stick flick for 90° camera turns.\n   - A per-letter dialog hook for the voices.\n   - A separate Voices audio bus.\n   - Three tools drawn on the character rig: a darning stick, a cobble club and the Seam Ripper.\n6. **One thing I would change:** a built-in voxel map type with its own depth-lift hook and occluder boxes.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the clear definition of done and the detailed plan. The controller-first, 10-foot rules made UI decisions easy.\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan's file names used another model and timestamp than TASK.md's.\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** proving the whole chapter completes through real triggers, while also building netcode and an attract mode.\n4. **What I would change:** a smaller slice or staged delivery. The scope is very large for one pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":653,"cache_read_input_tokens":891307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":653},"output_tokens":757,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2","uuid":"f35c515d-f0e5-488e-96b4-08cd650bfc29","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:21:01.228Z","request_id":"req_011CghUzbC2ZryzEyjWHBuQH"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The HTML and exit-interview.json exist, the exit interview parses, the final reply contains all four sections, and the last full run was 352 passed with no TODO/placeholder/stub hits. But TASK.md requires every feature implemented, and the transcript does not establish that. Several items were verified only by checks added or reworked after failing (the Bee 'won' check was changed, and the Knot Cutter award check was added late), and the full playthrough's clean pass and the final single-command run are separate runs. Some features, such as the Dev Tools World and Debug tabs and the Quilted Vest use, got their checks only in the final pass. Whether every TASK.md feature works end to end is not established by the transcript."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2","uuid":"24773422-a8f3-4f97-930d-7ae6660ec40f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:21:03.874Z","isSynthetic":true}
